WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.128 line:86%
In Vizai we have a tools tab

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:05.221 line:86%
with several handy features.

00:00:05.261 --> 00:00:06.579 line:86%
The first one I'll show

00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:08.447 line:86%
you optimizes the size and weight

00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:09.300 line:86%
of your file.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.085 line:86%
In it you can remove duplicated

00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:12.893 line:86%
textures,

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:14.780 line:86%
shrink those textures

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.724 line:86%
you import way too large,

00:00:16.764 --> 00:00:19.640 line:86%
and also use a feature called Impact.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.928 line:86%
With it you can spot which

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.700 line:86%
blocks have the most polygons and then

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.165 line:86%
decide whether it's really worth

00:00:27.205 --> 00:00:28.360 line:86%
replacing them.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.896 line:86%
As you can see,

00:00:43.936 --> 00:00:45.831 line:86%
these are all the textures

00:00:45.871 --> 00:00:47.840 line:86%
inside the project, and now

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.708 line:86%
we'll optimize all of them in

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:50.640 line:86%
a few clicks.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.193 line:86%
After optimizing,

00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:02.912 line:86%
just save,

00:01:02.952 --> 00:01:05.430 line:86%
and up top the file size is already

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:06.810 line:86%
updated to the new size.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.489 line:86%
Here you see every block placed

00:01:14.529 --> 00:01:15.685 line:86%
in your scene,

00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:16.540 line:86%
so you can

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.383 line:86%
check which ones weigh the most

00:01:18.423 --> 00:01:20.108 line:86%
and decide if they are really

00:01:20.148 --> 00:01:20.980 line:86%
worth keeping.

